{"model":"nomic-embed-text:latest","input":["river survey sample custody: the water chemistry kit stores unrelated reagents.","river survey sample custody: the field notebook marks another transect.","river survey sample custody: the vehicle shed keeps a separate fuel receipt.","river survey sample custody: the archive drive stores another survey export.","river survey sample custody: the safety briefing lists an unrelated hazard.","river survey sample custody: the spare cooler has another inventory tag.","river survey sample custody: the research office files a different grant note.","river sample custody: the river survey office files an unrelated equipment return.","river survey sample custody source record: River survey cooler RS-12 contains the north-bank water samples. Cooler RS-12 is handed from the boat crew to the lab courier at marker 6. The custody seal for cooler RS-12 is recorded as seal RIV-904.","river survey sample custody source note: the south-bank sediment bags use another accession range.","river survey sample custody source note: the survey boat stores a separate oar inspection card.","river survey sample custody source note: the lab freezer keeps an unrelated rack map.","river survey sample custody source note: the river gauge reports a different water level.","river survey sample custody source note: the field tablet carries another charging cable.","river survey sample custody source note: the permit folder contains an unrelated sampling waiver.","river survey sample custody source note: the wader kit is dried on a separate rack."],"truncate":false}